<HelpLayout title="Get started" active="get-started" description="Get up and running with Folio AI in a few minutes — install in PowerPoint or Google Slides and create your first deck.">
  <p>
    Welcome to Folio AI — the AI agent built for decks where every slide counts. Folio works
    directly inside <strong>PowerPoint</strong> and <strong>Google Slides</strong>, generating new
    presentations from a prompt and editing your existing decks while preserving your templates,
    fonts, and brand. This page walks you through everything you need to get started.
  </p>

  <h2>A quick overview</h2>
  <p>
    New to Folio? Watch this short walkthrough to see how to install Folio and create your first
    deck in just a few minutes.
  </p>
  <HelpMedia type="video" caption="Overview video: setting up Folio AI and generating your first presentation." />

  <h2>Install Folio AI</h2>
  <p>Folio runs as an add-in inside the presentation tools you already use. Pick your platform:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/help/powerpoint/">Use Folio AI in PowerPoint</a> — install the add-in on Windows, Mac, or PowerPoint on the web.</li>
    <li><a href="/help/google-slides/">Use Folio AI in Google Slides</a> — install the add-on from the Google Workspace Marketplace.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    There's nothing to download to your computer — Folio installs directly into PowerPoint or Google
    Slides and appears in a side panel next to your slides.
  </p>

  <h2>What is Folio AI?</h2>
  <p>
    Folio is an AI agent that works <em>with</em> you on your slides, not a separate app you export
    from. Once installed, you can:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Prompt to deck</strong> — describe what you need and Folio generates a full presentation, applying your existing template's fonts, colors, and layouts automatically.</li>
    <li><strong>Edit an existing deck</strong> — open any presentation and ask Folio to restructure, rewrite, reformat, or extend it. Folio works with real PowerPoint and Google Slides shapes, so every element stays fully editable.</li>
    <li><strong>Rewrite and restyle content</strong> — adjust tone, length, or audience, and let Folio rework the wording across slides.</li>
    <li><strong>Upload your own files</strong> — drop in a logo, image, data, or an inspiration deck, and Folio will use it as context for your prompt.</li>
  </ul>
  <HelpMedia caption="Screenshot: the Folio side panel open alongside a slide in PowerPoint." />

  <h2>Start for free</h2>
  <p>
    Every new account starts with <strong>500 free credits</strong> and <strong>no credit card
    required</strong>. Credits are what you spend when Folio generates or edits slides — a complete
    10-slide deck typically uses 100–200 credits. When you're ready for more, see
    <a href="/help/plans-and-billing/">Plans and Billing</a>.
  </p>

